# Manual transaction edits (admin) — persist on refresh

## Fields edited in Transaction History

| Field | Persist target | Survive reload |
|-------|----------------|----------------|
| Category | Statement History row(s) + cache | `confidence: Manual` skips auto re-classify |
| Department | same | same |
| Date / amount | same | patched via soft amount+description match |
| GST claim / FREE | same | `gstInfo.reasoning` starts with `Manual:` |
| FBT flag | same | written with other Manual fields |
| Cash expense rows | `cashExpenses` store | by `cash_*` id |

## Invariants

1. Write bank edits into **every** History statement that contains the row — not only `currentStatementId`.
2. Never let `applyKnownExpenseCategoriesIfMissing` overwrite `Manual` / `Learned` categories.
3. Never let `applyKnownPurchaseGstTags` overwrite `Manual:` GST tags.
4. Sync `accounting_transactions` cache after a successful edit.

## Do not

- Persist only when the user clicked Load on that PDF first
- Re-run strong company rules on Manual rows after refresh
